         <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193118_306906_23606"
                          xmi:uuid="7b7a4e3c-a511-426e-8177-f01289f5f286"
                          xmi:type="uml:Class">
            <name xmlns:sysml="http://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20150709/SysML"
                  xmlns:StandardProfile="http://www.omg.org/spec/UML/20131001/StandardProfile">Identifier</name>
            <ownedRule xmlns:sysml="http://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20150709/SysML"
                       xmlns:StandardProfile="http://www.omg.org/spec/UML/20131001/StandardProfile"
                       xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1594974158696_973578_99916"
                       xmi:uuid="766428c3-2b76-4cd2-9164-0e66cde664b0"
                       xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1599724998095_541275_89446"
                             xmi:uuid="67019df2-9042-4710-a83b-a2178cc2f823"
                             xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_271a0567_1594974158696_973578_99916"/>
                  <body>An instance of the entity Identifier used in the role Id or VersionId of any other entity shall be unique along id, role and context over all instances of the entity (for example over all instances of Part, all instances of Document, …). To be applied successfully on VersionId being unique only in combination with Id, the context of the VersionId shall refer to one of the Ids (for example given an instance #1 of Part.Id: PartVersion.id.identificationContext shall refer to #1). </body>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>IP1</name>
               <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193118_306906_23606"/>
               <specification xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1594974158697_656988_99917"
                              xmi:uuid="abc641b3-ca0e-4a96-8513-3e56f440c58f"
                              xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
                  <body>An instance of the entity Identifier used in the role Id or VersionId of any other entity shall be unique along id, role and context over all instances of the entity (for example over all instances of Part, all instances of Document, …). To be applied successfully on VersionId being unique only in combination with Id, the context of the VersionId shall refer to one of the Ids (for example given an instance #1 of Part.Id: PartVersion.id.identificationContext shall refer to #1). </body>
                  <language>English</language>
               </specification>
            </ownedRule>
