         </packagedElement>
         <packagedElement xmlns:sysml="http://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20150709/SysML"
                          xmlns:StandardProfile="http://www.omg.org/spec/UML/20131001/StandardProfile"
                          xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193297_520470_23930"
                          xmi:uuid="a018ae91-6946-44e1-a1ef-226dbe383812"
                          xmi:type="uml:Enumeration">
            <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456299362277_886341_42885"
                          xmi:uuid="2e9468d1-fa48-4076-9ea7-7bb18992e564"
                          xmi:type="uml:Comment">
               <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193297_520470_23930"/>
               <body>A HighOrderKinematicPairTypeEnum type lists the possible types of a HighOrderKinematicPair. The constraints of these pair types shall follow the mathematical definition provided in ISO 10303-105. </body>
            </ownedComment>
            <name>HighOrderKinematicPairTypeEnum</name>
            <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194143_538447_29291"
                          xmi:uuid="f94b8f08-74f6-4b20-883e-f411fedf2620"
                          xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456299386256_428308_42886"
                             xmi:uuid="749f1752-4b75-4d7e-8751-38362aa22f23"
                             xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194143_538447_29291"/>
                  <body> the pair describes a linear flexible link that moves around a rolling pinion where the rotation axis of the pinion is perpendicular to the direction of the linear flexible link.</body>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>linear_flexible_and_planar_curve_pair</name>
            </ownedLiteral>
            <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194143_489193_29292"
                          xmi:uuid="5a04a811-38ec-4919-9316-33c0023d88d7"
                          xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456299400078_372556_42887"
                             xmi:uuid="3e9abefa-847b-4ea9-879a-f2d2b9bc2ef4"
                             xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194143_489193_29292"/>
                  <body> the pair constrains the motion of two links such that a point defined on the second link always lies on a surface defined on the first link. The actual location of this point on the surface is called the contact point. The contact point specifies an origin of a frame called the contact frame. The local normal to the surface in the contact point coincides with the z-axis of the contact frame. The x-axis of the contact frame is parallel to the tangent to the iso-parameter line of the surface for the first surface parameter, which passes the contact point, and points into the direction where the first surface parameter increases.</body>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>point_on_surface_pair</name>
            </ownedLiteral>
            <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194143_560365_29293"
                          xmi:uuid="c6609109-adcf-40aa-810e-6fc20529f412"
                          xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456299412941_232916_42888"
                             xmi:uuid="2350a6df-7e53-4d31-aeb6-bfb7559da50c"
                             xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194143_560365_29293"/>
                  <body> a pair that constrains the motion of two links such that a point defined on the second link always lies on a planar curve defined on the first link. The actual location of this point on the curve is called the contact point.</body>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>point_on_planar_curve_pair</name>
            </ownedLiteral>
            <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194144_334385_29294"
                          xmi:uuid="601ca56e-166c-4007-9ed2-181fc7dfe3df"
                          xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456299424436_1424_42889"
                             xmi:uuid="48327c40-56cf-4b40-a3fc-43a999b7edea"
                             xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194144_334385_29294"/>
                  <body> a pair that constrains the motion of two links along a planar curve on each of the links. Both curves lie in a common plane.</body>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>planar_curve_pair</name>
            </ownedLiteral>
            <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194144_236425_29295"
                          xmi:uuid="d10f447d-a411-4fa6-881f-0cb6e76d657f"
                          xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456299440920_548279_42890"
                             xmi:uuid="87874db3-9cd3-48f2-8e2e-4a751d29c254"
                             xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194144_236425_29295"/>
                  <body> a kind of a Planar_curve_pair that specifies the rolling motion between the curves on the two links.</body>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>rolling_curve_pair</name>
            </ownedLiteral>
            <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194144_374510_29296"
                          xmi:uuid="9670dd8c-8455-41b2-a1e5-cff8cd19f3b4"
                          xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456299453726_310177_42891"
                             xmi:uuid="47c03fb4-6b7d-417a-80b0-878f5fcf8da5"
                             xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194144_374510_29296"/>
                  <body> a kind of a Planar_curve_pair that specifies the sliding motion between the curves on the two links.</body>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>sliding_curve_pair</name>
            </ownedLiteral>
            <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194144_386850_29297"
                          xmi:uuid="1ca5de0b-d5bd-452f-a3b2-08427190e247"
                          xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456299464194_739575_42892"
                             xmi:uuid="f2a94a10-d5ae-42df-9366-bda385b43454"
                             xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194144_386850_29297"/>
                  <body> a pair that specifies a rolling motion between the two contact surfaces on the two links.</body>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>rolling_surface_pair</name>
            </ownedLiteral>
            <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194144_423858_29298"
                          xmi:uuid="331ed739-42ee-409c-8a89-75defd812759"
                          xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456299472714_819886_42893"
                             xmi:uuid="e9926f6c-3f67-49a4-a387-cf1eb35c6962"
                             xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194144_423858_29298"/>
                  <body> a pair that specifies the a sliding between the two contact surfaces on the two links.</body>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>sliding_surface_pair</name>
            </ownedLiteral>
         </packagedElement>
         <packagedElement xmlns:sysml="http://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20150709/SysML"
                          xmlns:StandardProfile="http://www.omg.org/spec/UML/20131001/StandardProfile"
                          xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1722963052616_971858_60243"
                          xmi:uuid="c43851e7-ff87-4ba7-a00d-94b33787cc16"
                          xmi:type="uml:Enumeration">
            <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1722963052633_609284_60250"
                          xmi:uuid="095285a9-51d6-41a5-9d45-b55ad528d856"
                          xmi:type="uml:Comment">
               <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_2840147_1722963052616_971858_60243"/>
               <body>A CouplingTypeEnum type lists the possible types for the kind of coupling.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <name>CouplingTypeEnum</name>
            <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1722963159754_804947_60260"
                          xmi:uuid="64c35525-8b76-454f-a63b-7b44c21a657b"
                          xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1727280623928_233342_151347"
                             xmi:uuid="77fda410-408d-413c-a3ed-2f71f84e092d"
                             xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_2840147_1722963159754_804947_60260"/>
                  <body>the pairs are coupled by a rotation.</body>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>rotation</name>
            </ownedLiteral>
            <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1722963307827_302146_60261"
                          xmi:uuid="7dd3d169-ae3f-4d0c-91cf-6e64a9a07b16"
                          xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1727280632460_116662_151348"
                             xmi:uuid="c5fe3197-f02d-4e07-845f-5fb80f950cb6"
                             xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_2840147_1722963307827_302146_60261"/>
                  <body>the pairs are coupled by a translation.</body>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>translation</name>
            </ownedLiteral>
         </packagedElement>
         <packagedElement xmlns:sysml="http://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/20150709/SysML"
                          xmlns:StandardProfile="http://www.omg.org/spec/UML/20131001/StandardProfile"
                          xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193304_660763_23943"
                          xmi:uuid="c47a972f-6e40-4278-8c42-6871c4c508c0"
                          xmi:type="uml:Enumeration">
            <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456299795224_927606_42914"
                          xmi:uuid="ae3bfd07-85ba-4e9d-b8b6-59a08dff9513"
                          xmi:type="uml:Comment">
               <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193304_660763_23943"/>
               <body>A TransitionCodeEnum is an enumeration that conveys the continuity properties of a motion along a PathSegment. The continuity referred to is geometric, not parametric continuity.</body>
            </ownedComment>
            <name>TransitionCodeEnum</name>
            <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1522143140858_69700_198518"
                            xmi:uuid="e4a71bda-7aa0-4827-b3bd-ba99e6c84520"
                            xmi:type="uml:Property">
               <name>arm_mapping</name>
               <visibility>private</visibility>
               <type href="../../../../SysML_ARM/SYSML_ARM_AP242.xmi#_SYSML_ARM-curve_transition_code"/>
               <isReadOnly>true</isReadOnly>
            </ownedAttribute>
            <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194167_491365_29466"
                          xmi:uuid="db898c3c-536e-4298-bd62-5c804302f645"
                          xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456299839955_279499_42915"
                             xmi:uuid="9354ba6c-ed93-40c7-aada-779dd86e0d2a"
                             xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194167_491365_29466"/>
                  <body> the motion segments join, and their tangent vectors are parallel and have the same direction at the joint; equality of derivatives is not required.</body>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>cont_same_gradient</name>
               <slot xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1522152548207_533363_200288"
                     xmi:uuid="6e7f360c-784e-4c2d-a15b-d51d004cccbc"
                     xmi:type="uml:Slot">
                  <definingFeature xmi:idref="_18_4_1_271a0567_1522143140858_69700_198518"/>
                  <value xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1522152548237_797595_200289"
                         xmi:uuid="f67d8046-862c-4d48-96dc-25e40dc6e3bb"
                         xmi:type="uml:InstanceValue">
                     <instance href="../../../../SysML_ARM/SYSML_ARM_AP242.xmi#_1_enumitem_SYSML_ARM-curve_transition_code-cont_same_gradient"/>
                  </value>
               </slot>
            </ownedLiteral>
            <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194167_753503_29467"
                          xmi:uuid="d6e2dfc4-acc0-4a6a-b307-340ca7d7805b"
                          xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456299851705_564020_42916"
                             xmi:uuid="dc9ec65d-3dae-413a-867c-08cd574d2174"
                             xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194167_753503_29467"/>
                  <body> the motion segments join, their tangent vectors are parallel and in the same direction, and their curvatures are equal at the joint; equality of derivatives is not required.</body>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>cont_same_gradient_same_curvature</name>
               <slot xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1522152573043_584736_200292"
                     xmi:uuid="38a5a790-d7b9-441c-9330-774f5e654b6f"
                     xmi:type="uml:Slot">
                  <definingFeature xmi:idref="_18_4_1_271a0567_1522143140858_69700_198518"/>
                  <value xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1522152573056_378546_200293"
                         xmi:uuid="dc74ecc8-ae10-4c93-bbab-0945aa297c7a"
                         xmi:type="uml:InstanceValue">
                     <instance href="../../../../SysML_ARM/SYSML_ARM_AP242.xmi#_1_enumitem_SYSML_ARM-curve_transition_code-cont_same_gradient_same_curvature"/>
                  </value>
               </slot>
            </ownedLiteral>
            <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194167_875118_29468"
                          xmi:uuid="816df20e-66cc-4399-b044-8893cf3f7a2a"
                          xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456299861039_348071_42917"
                             xmi:uuid="4223ec0e-fa1c-4428-ad97-1f1fc282ebc8"
                             xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194167_875118_29468"/>
                  <body> the motion segments join, but no condition on their tangents is implied.</body>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>continuous</name>
               <slot xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1522152586639_32194_200296"
                     xmi:uuid="0b902605-f5c0-4228-8f9a-4806ef285103"
                     xmi:type="uml:Slot">
                  <definingFeature xmi:idref="_18_4_1_271a0567_1522143140858_69700_198518"/>
                  <value xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1522152586650_614280_200297"
                         xmi:uuid="5953c0ac-b36c-4bdf-9d19-0dfbf9ae5911"
                         xmi:type="uml:InstanceValue">
                     <instance href="../../../../SysML_ARM/SYSML_ARM_AP242.xmi#_1_enumitem_SYSML_ARM-curve_transition_code-continuous"/>
                  </value>
               </slot>
            </ownedLiteral>
            <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194167_238802_29469"
                          xmi:uuid="14e7b4b3-1073-4da6-827f-de77c1c00498"
                          xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456299871223_24218_42918"
                             xmi:uuid="db6f0f22-6543-4687-95b9-12894e6ea453"
                             xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417194167_238802_29469"/>
                  <body> the motion segments do not join; the motion is interrupted.</body>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>discontinuous</name>
               <slot xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1522152608035_199789_200300"
                     xmi:uuid="ba1c43e8-21d3-47c7-ad6d-097a2a2b2bb0"
                     xmi:type="uml:Slot">
                  <definingFeature xmi:idref="_18_4_1_271a0567_1522143140858_69700_198518"/>
                  <value xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1522152608045_672938_200301"
                         xmi:uuid="734232de-a129-49fc-9070-6293f3baa9a8"
                         xmi:type="uml:InstanceValue">
                     <instance href="../../../../SysML_ARM/SYSML_ARM_AP242.xmi#_1_enumitem_SYSML_ARM-curve_transition_code-discontinuous"/>
                  </value>
